From 0c4d936b167f2fb0786d9f424d1c5e2fe32d106a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:44:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] [Bugfix][KV Cache] Decline a Mamba checkpoint grid that
 grows the block

Serving geometry PP=4 TP=1 sm80, qwen4_exp, fp8 KV, --block-size 1616,
--mamba-cache-mode align, --prefix-match-unit 16, MTP-4 resolved its KV
groups to (3232, 3232, 3232, 3232, 8, 3232) on bases up to e72e9cb18 and
to (6464, ...) from db8e4658ed on. The doubling is computed, not
preferred. Phase 1 of Platform.update_block_size_for_backend (the code
2440ffc387 changed, which the bisect blamed) never runs for this geometry:
an explicit --block-size sets user_specified_block_size and skips it.

Two inputs inside Platform._align_hybrid_block_size decide the number.

1. Page floor. A one-byte fp8 KV page holds half the bytes per token of
   the bf16 page 1616 was sized against, so the block rounds up to the
   Mamba state page: 1616 * ceil(mamba_page / (1616 * attn_page)) = 3232.
   That is where 3232 comes from: twice the pinned block, a multiple of
   the QSA kernel's MultipleOf(16) (models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py) and of
   the 8-token QSA indexer ring, round_up(compress_ratio 4 + 4 speculative
   rows, 4) (models/qwen4_exp/common/qsa_indexer.py). The group LCM stays
   3232, so a retention interval of 12928 tokens is a whole number of
   scheduler steps.
2. Checkpoint grid. 29c6cfc457 gave the Triton/FLA GDN prefill a prefill
   checkpoint alignment of FLA_CHUNK_SIZE = 64, where previously only the
   FlashInfer prefill declared one, and the same function LCMs that grid
   into the block: lcm(1616, 64) = 6464. The grid has to divide the block,
   otherwise a block boundary sits off the stride the kernel emits states
   on and an exported state cannot be resumed from.

CPU reproduction of that function (real Qwen4Exp model class, real QSA
backend, stub Mamba layer): grid None -> 3232, 64 -> 6464, 128 -> 12928.
The resolved block tracks lcm(pinned block, grid), which also covers the
1616 -> 3232 -> 6464 history across bases.

6464 costs the lane: retention and the grown-turn grid coarsen 2x, and
prefill chunk ends stop landing on the block (9728 gives 9696-row chunks,
a multiple of 3232 and not of 6464). The grid is an optimization, so make
it declineable.

Add Platform.get_mamba_checkpoint_grid, the single place where the
platform decides whether the layers' grid may grow the KV block, and route
get_mamba_prefill_checkpoint_alignment through it. With
VLLM_MAMBA_CHECKPOINT_BLOCK_PIN=1 the platform declines a grid the block is
not on. The layers read the same function, so they stop exporting internal
checkpoints, the scheduler resumes splitting prefills as it did before
29c6cfc457, and the block stays at the page floor. Off by default, which
leaves every other configuration untouched, including the upstream tests
that guard the grid. A platform wanting a different policy overrides the
method.

The gate that enables internal checkpoints is `cache_config.enable_prefix_caching` (9a4930a797 dropped the `mamba_cache_mode == "align"` check), so the tests set that.

CPU suites (tests/models/qwen4_exp, tests/v1/core KV cache and mamba align,
tests/v1/attention block size and backend selection, tests/models/step5):
416 -> 428 passed, 196 skipped, 0 failed. The new
tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_kv_block_size_pin.py covers the mechanism, the
veto table, and the group and retention arithmetic.
